cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TriZOD: Re-referenced BMRB chemical shift dataset and disorder scoring pipeline"
message: >-
  If you use the TriZOD dataset, please cite it as below. The dataset is
  licensed CC BY 4.0; the code in this repository is MIT (see LICENSE).
  The data derive from BMRB entries (https://bmrb.io); please also
  acknowledge the BMRB.
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  Per-residue protein-disorder labels (the continuous TriZOD G-score) from
  re-referenced BMRB NMR backbone chemical shifts, one Parquet row per scored
  protein chain, in four nested stringency tiers, with the held-out test set
  TriZOD-test v1.0 and CheZOD117. Training sets are separated from the test
  sets at 30 % identity over 80 % of either chain, searched in both
  directions.
